## Add opt-in hierarchy instance IRI scope (issue #228)

Context: A parent class and a subclass mapped with the same business id produced
two unlinked Knowledge Graph nodes, because instance URIs embed the mapped class
name ({base}{Class}/{id}) and inherited relations (#43) stay on the declaring
class URI. A new domain setting mints root-class URIs so both mappings land on one
node carrying every type and relationship.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/w3c/r2rml/InstanceIdentity.py
   New pure helper: scope normalization, root-class segment map, sibling collision detection.
2. src/back/core/w3c/r2rml/__init__.py
   Re-export InstanceIdentity.
3. src/back/core/w3c/r2rml/R2RMLGenerator.py
   Entity and relationship templates use the root-class segment in hierarchy scope.
4. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/query/TwinMapping.py
   Fallback URI templates follow the same root-class segment.
5. src/back/objects/domain/Domain.py
   Save identity_scope on the ontology, reset generated R2RML, expose it to UI.
6. src/back/objects/session/DomainSession.py
   Export identity_scope with the ontology.
7. src/back/objects/mapping/Mapping.py
   Diagnostics warn when unrelated mapped classes share a root.
8. src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_information.html, src/front/static/domain/js/domain.js,
   src/front/static/global/js/navbar.js, src/front/static/domain/js/domain-information.js
   Instance IRI scope selector, save payload and refresh.
9. src/front/static/query/js/query-loaders.js, src/front/static/query/js/query-d3graph.js
   Explorer keeps the most specific rdf:type of multi-typed nodes.
10. docs/user-guide.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/advanced_features.md
    Document the instance IRI scope.
11. tests/units/mapping/test_instance_identity.py, tests/units/mapping/test_r2rml_generator.py,
    tests/units/dtwin/test_v090_twin_mapping.py, tests/units/domain/test_domain_service.py,
    tests/units/domain/test_domain_session.py, tests/units/mapping/test_mapping_service.py,
    tests/units/front/test_identity_scope_ui.py
    Unit coverage for root minting, persistence, diagnostics, and UI contracts.

